  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">START Learning Grant for India Flooding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD and co-lead agencies (including Caritas India) seek to undertake a study on the various mechanisms in place for ensuring accountability to affected population within emergency responses to flooding in India, using as case studies Start Alert funded responses in Kerala and Odisha. The objectives are to:
&#x2022;	Identify gaps by reviewing existing accountability practices, standards, and frameworks.
&#x2022;	Document best practices in ensuring accountability. 
The study should go a long way in acting as a guideline/tool for various stakeholders in future disaster responses to ensure highest grade of accountability to the affected community.</narrative>
  </description>
